.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# build/ is deliberately NOT ignored. The built simulator.html and index.html are the
# deployable artifact: a static host serves build/ as the site root with no build step.
# Ignoring it would mean the repository could not be deployed from a clone.

# The Claude desktop app drops files it delivers into the conversation here. They are
# screenshots and scratch, not repository content.
Claude outputs/

# node_modules/ holds one thing: @huggingface/transformers, which
# engine/matcher_eval.mjs needs for its --semantic arm and nothing else does. It is a
# development dependency of one evaluation tool and no part of the product: the built
# simulator loads its own copy of the library from a CDN at runtime and never reads this
# directory. package.json records the version so `npm install` reproduces it.
#
# package-lock.json is NOT ignored, so the version the numbers were measured against is
# in the repository even though the tree is not.
node_modules/
